---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";

const description = "A fictional monthly content example for an invented Arlington counseling practice, showing how practical website, social, and email copy can work together.";

const posts = [
	["Instagram · 01 / 12", "Before you choose an appointment format, ask what will make the first visit easier to attend: location, timing, privacy, or a mix of those details. Our practical guide explains the questions to bring to the office."],
	["LinkedIn · 02 / 12", "Before sharing a practice’s details with someone, check the service area and the current inquiry route. For Harbor & Pine Counseling, start with our practice information page and contact the office to confirm availability. A listing alone does not confirm an opening."],
	["Instagram · 03 / 12", "Planning a first call? Write down the days and times you are generally available, your preferred appointment format, and any access questions. Having those details ready can make an inquiry more straightforward."],
	["LinkedIn · 04 / 12", "A referral can begin with an information request. Professional contacts can ask Harbor & Pine Counseling about services, appointment formats, and current availability before sharing our public contact page. Please keep personal client details out of social messages."],
	["Instagram · 05 / 12", "Before you book, ask the office to confirm the current fee, payment options, and cancellation terms for the appointment you are considering. If something on the website is unclear, it is okay to ask for the details in writing."],
	["LinkedIn · 06 / 12", "Have an older copy of our practice information? Use the current public page when sharing Harbor & Pine Counseling’s details. Services, availability, and contact instructions can change. The office can confirm the next step before an appointment is arranged."],
];

const articleSchema = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "Article",
	headline: "A Month of Content for a Therapy Practice",
	description,
	datePublished: "2026-09-08",
	author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Elaren Studio", url: "https://elarenstudio.com" },
	publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Elaren Studio", url: "https://elarenstudio.com" },
	mainEntityOfPage: "https://elarenstudio.com/work-examples/private-practice-content/",
};
---

<BaseLayout title="A Month of Content for a Therapy Practice" description={description} ogType="article" articleDate="2026-09-08">
	<Header />
	<main>
		<section class="container py-8 md:py-12"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Private practice marketing", href: "/private-practice-marketing" }, { label: "Private practice content" }]} /></section>
		<section class="container pb-16 md:pb-24"><div class="max-w-3xl">
			<p class="mb-3 text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">Content marketing / work example</p>
			<h1 class="mb-6 text-4xl font-semibold text-ink md:text-5xl">A Month of Content for a Therapy Practice</h1>
			<p class="mb-5 text-sm text-ink/60">By Elaren Studio · September 8, 2026</p>
			<div class="rounded-xl border-2 border-accent/30 bg-accent/5 p-5 text-ink"><strong>Fictional demonstration:</strong> Harbor &amp; Pine Counseling is an invented Arlington practice for this example. It is not Wright Wellness, a client, a testimonial, a clinical recommendation, or a claim of results. Services, credentials, fees, availability, and service area would be verified with the practice before publication.</div>
			<p class="mt-6 text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink/80">A practice owner does not need twelve versions of the same announcement. This sample shows a month organized around useful office logistics: choosing an appointment format, understanding the inquiry path, and keeping public details current.</p>
			<a href="/private-practice-marketing#inquiry" class="mt-7 inline-flex rounded-xl bg-accent px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-paper no-underline shadow-lg shadow-accent/30">Discuss content for my practice</a>
		</div></section>

		<section class="bg-[var(--clr-muted)] py-16 md:py-20"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl"><h2 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">The monthly map</h2><p class="leading-relaxed text-ink/75">One approved topic map keeps the writing useful and gives the owner clear review points. The package below follows the existing content marketing scope.</p></div>
			<div class="mt-8 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
				<div class="rounded-xl border-2 border-slate-200 bg-paper p-6"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent">Website · 2 pieces</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Answer the practical questions</h3><p class="mt-3 text-ink/70">Two articles or existing-page updates, each up to 1,000 words, cover appointment format, fees, availability, and how an inquiry works.</p></div>
				<div class="rounded-xl border-2 border-slate-200 bg-paper p-6"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent">Social · 12 posts</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Repeat the point with a new angle</h3><p class="mt-3 text-ink/70">Twelve original posts are adapted across the practice’s existing Instagram and LinkedIn accounts. Six finished excerpts appear below.</p></div>
				<div class="rounded-xl border-2 border-slate-200 bg-paper p-6"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent">Email · 1 campaign</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Give referrers a current reference</h3><p class="mt-3 text-ink/70">One plain-text email, up to 500 words, is written for opt-in professional referral contacts and links to approved public information.</p></div>
				<div class="rounded-xl border-2 border-slate-200 bg-paper p-6"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent">Rationale</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Make review manageable</h3><p class="mt-3 text-ink/70">Each piece has a small job: reduce uncertainty, show the next question to ask, or help a professional contact find accurate logistics.</p></div>
			</div>
		</div></section>

		<section class="container py-16 md:py-24"><div class="max-w-4xl"><h2 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Article one: choosing an appointment format</h2><p class="mb-7 text-ink/75">Substantive outline for an article of no more than 1,000 words. It stays with office logistics and prompts the reader to verify current details with the practice.</p>
			<div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr]"><article class="rounded-xl border-2 border-slate-200 bg-paper p-7"><h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">What to ask before choosing an appointment format</h3><p class="mt-4 text-ink/75">Practical details are part of choosing an appointment format. Before you contact a practice, note which days and times are realistic, whether you are comparing an office visit with a remote option, and what questions you want answered first.</p><h4 class="mt-6 text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Start with the logistics you can name</h4><p class="mt-3 text-ink/75">Ask where the office is located, how appointments are requested, what the current availability looks like, and whether the practice offers the format you are considering. If fees or payment information are not clear on the website, ask the practice directly for the current details.</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink/60">Opening excerpt only. The finished article would use the practice’s approved services, fee language, availability, access notes, and inquiry route.</p></article>
				<div class="rounded-xl border-2 border-slate-200 p-7"><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Outline</h3><ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5 text-ink/75"><li>Compare office and remote logistics without assuming either is available.</li><li>List the questions to ask about timing, location, access, and privacy.</li><li>Explain what information helps a practice respond to an inquiry.</li><li>Point readers to the approved services, fees, and availability pages.</li><li>Close with a plain-text invitation to ask the practice a question.</li></ol><p class="mt-6 text-sm text-ink/60"><strong>Buyer rationale:</strong> A clear outline lets the owner approve the factual inputs before the prose is expanded.</p></div></div>
		</div></section>

		<section class="bg-[var(--clr-muted)] py-16 md:py-20"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-4xl"><h2 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Article two: existing-page update</h2><p class="mb-7 text-ink/75">A shorter update keeps the practice’s inquiry page aligned with the facts the owner has approved.</p><article class="rounded-xl border-2 border-slate-200 bg-paper p-7"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">Page update excerpt · “Before you contact Harbor &amp; Pine”</p><p class="mt-4 text-ink/80">You can start with a few practical details: the service you are asking about, the days or times that may work, and whether you are asking about an office or remote appointment. Harbor &amp; Pine Counseling will confirm current availability, fees, and next steps directly. If you are unsure which question to ask, send the simplest version of what you need to know.</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink/60"><strong>Buyer rationale:</strong> Updating an existing page can make the next step clearer without creating a new claim or promising an outcome.</p></article></div></div></section>

		<section class="container py-16 md:py-24"><div class="max-w-4xl"><h2 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Six finished posts from the twelve-post batch</h2><p class="mb-7 text-ink/75">These are finished excerpts from the month, adapted for two existing platforms. The other six posts would complete the approved map; this page does not present the full delivery.</p><ol class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">{posts.map(([angle, post]) => <li class="rounded-xl border-2 border-slate-200 bg-paper p-5"><span class="text-sm font-semibold text-accent">{angle}</span><p class="mt-2 text-ink/75">{post}</p><p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink/55"><strong>Why it helps:</strong> A small, answerable question gives the practice a useful reason to publish.</p></li>)}</ol></div></section>

		<section class="bg-[var(--clr-muted)] py-16 md:py-20"><div class="container"><div class="max-w-3xl"><h2 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Email for opt-in professional referral contacts</h2><p class="mb-7 text-ink/75">Plain-text example, under 500 words. It assumes the practice has an approved contact list and a verified public page to link.</p><article class="rounded-xl border-2 border-slate-200 bg-paper p-7 text-ink/80"><p><strong>Subject:</strong> Current practice information from Harbor &amp; Pine Counseling</p><hr class="my-5 border-slate-200" /><p>Hello,</p><p class="mt-4">I’m sharing a current reference for Harbor &amp; Pine Counseling in Arlington. The practice’s public information covers available services, appointment format questions, and how to ask about current fees and availability.</p><p class="mt-4">If someone in your professional network asks for logistics, please direct them to the practice’s approved information page: <span class="text-accent">[verified practice URL]</span>. They can use the inquiry route there to ask a question or request the next step.</p><p class="mt-4">Thank you for keeping this reference on hand.</p><p class="mt-4">Harbor &amp; Pine Counseling<br />[verified practice contact details]</p><p class="mt-5 font-semibold">CTA: View the current practice information</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink/60">Demonstration copy only. No referral relationship, contact list, form, or appointment request is created by this page.</p></article><p class="mt-5 text-sm text-ink/60"><strong>Buyer rationale:</strong> A short reference email helps approved professional contacts find facts without using a patient story, testimonial, or clinical promise.</p></div></div></section>

		<section class="container py-16 md:py-24"><div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2"><div><h2 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Approval checklist</h2><ul class="space-y-3 text-ink/75"><li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span>Practice verifies services, credentials, fees, availability, and service area.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span>Owner approves the appointment-format language, inquiry route, links, and any supplied assets.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span>A practice clinician reviews any clinical claim if one is added later.</span></li><li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-accent" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><span>Practice confirms the opt-in referral list and approved scheduling window.</span></li></ul></div><div><h2 class="mb-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Scope boundaries</h2><p class="leading-relaxed text-ink/75">This package can design from supplied assets and schedule approved copy in existing systems. It does not include filming, photo shoots, paid ads or ad spend, daily community management, new tools, or a technical SEO campaign. Scheduling is performed only after approval.</p><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink/75">The sample contains no patient stories, testimonials, PHI, invented staff credentials, clinical advice, or outcome claims.</p></div></div></section>

		<section class="container border-t border-slate-100 py-12"><p class="text-sm text-ink/65">See the <a href="/content-marketing" class="text-accent hover:underline">content marketing scope</a> or the <a href="/resources/teardowns/wright-wellness-before-after-teardown" class="text-accent hover:underline">Wright Wellness website case study</a>. Both are separate from this fictional example.</p></section>
	</main>
	<Footer />
	<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />
</BaseLayout>
